{"id": "EUVD-2026-94308", "enisaUuid": "ecef821b-473f-39a5-858b-758afd6816bb", "description": "MiniUPnPd through 2.3.11 built with --strict contains a divide-by-zero vulnerability in ProcessSSDPData() that allows unauthenticated local network attackers to crash the daemon. Attackers can send a single multicast M-SEARCH datagram with MX: 0 and a known ST to port 1900, triggering SIGFPE and denying UPnP IGD service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-07T11:59:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-07T17:43:23", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp/commit/8f13b7a5843f5270db684099c0a083f98869636a", "https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp", "https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp/blob/miniupnpd_2_3_11/miniupnpd/minissdp.c#L1143-L1158", "https://github.com/miniupnp/miniupnp/blob/miniupnpd_2_3_11/miniupnpd/minissdp.c#L1281", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/miniupnpd-through-2.3.11-divide-by-zero-dos-via-ssdp-m-search-mx-header"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-107159", "GHSA-57wm-f7xc-rw5q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c9b7862b-a481-3560-a089-e5d314adbc2d", "product": {"name": "miniupnpd", "vendor": {"name": "miniupnp project"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.3.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d98038b5-5169-37af-be8a-9377faff0181", "vendor": {"name": "miniupnp project"}}], "isExploited": false}